# The helmet and the suit lamp by hand: a grip on the right side of the helmet opens or closes it, a grip on the left side
# switches the suit lamp. The plugin reads the game's own state back into its log a moment after each grip.
# Needs: Earth Planet; Options > VR > Display > Helmet view on, Controls > Helmet and lamp by hand on (the defaults).
# The hands are placed from the head: the helmet's middle is 9 cm behind the eyes, its shell reaches 26 cm from there.
plugin SpaceEngineersVR
world game:Earth Planet
log SpaceEngineersVR.log
expect session focused within 60

head 0 1.6 0
wait 2
# the game's exposure moves the whole view for a while after a load: the images below are compared once it has settled
expect headset steady

# before: nothing is gripped
headset helmet-b.png
expect no log Helmet and lamp by hand: Right helmet grip

# the right hand to the right side of the helmet, grip: the helmet opens or closes (whichever it was not)
hand right 0.12 1.59 0.09
wait 0.7
press right grip
wait 0.8
release right grip
wait 1.5
headset helmet-toggled.png
expect headset changed
expect log Helmet and lamp by hand: Right helmet grip -> helmet within 5

# and again: the other way
hand right 0.12 1.59 0.09
wait 0.5
press right grip
wait 0.8
release right grip
wait 1.5
headset helmet-toggled-back.png
expect headset changed
expect log -> helmet off within 5
expect log -> helmet on within 5

# the left hand to the left side of the helmet, grip: the suit lamp switches
hand left -0.12 1.59 0.09
wait 0.7
press left grip
wait 0.8
release left grip
wait 1
expect log Helmet and lamp by hand: Left lamp grip -> lamp within 5

# and again: the other way
hand left -0.12 1.59 0.09
wait 0.5
press left grip
wait 0.8
release left grip
wait 1
expect log -> lamp on within 5
expect log -> lamp off within 5
